+      "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane156": "PIN ADVANCED 7ebcbb0b6 -> d14e36827 (feature/turboquant-kv-cache, 2026-08-18). THE TAIL IS 3 COMMITS, reviewed one by one. TAKEN: 730cc87ed 'moe-cache: heat-protected eviction keeps hot experts resident' - full pools now evict the LRU expert whose resident hit count is at or below *_MOE_CACHE_HOT_USES (default 4) before touching a hotter one. The provider-agnostic half is ggml/src/ggml-moe-cache-common.h (+37/-1) and the Vulkan provider - the only one this rig builds - picks it up in 7 lines; CUDA and Metal land unbuilt on the standing 2026-08-18 HQ off-rig ruling. Its doc follow-up cef75bf06 folded into the same take. Taken at TIP state because all four code files were BYTE-IDENTICAL to the previous pin beforehand, so tip and delta are the same bytes; docs/backend/MOE-CACHE.md was 2 lines BEHIND the pin (the 1 GiB auto slab-floor paragraph) and tip restores it, which is why its numstat reads 6/1 not 3/1. Measured-effect UNMEASURED here: the source reports +12% TG (soft) / +7.5% (auto) on an RTX 5090 with Laguna S-2.1, a CUDA measurement on hardware this estate does not have - quoted, NOT adopted. Commit 92e2f0c01. DECLINED, LOUDLY: d14e36827 'docs: allow AI-assisted contribution workflows' touches AGENTS.md ONLY (24/74) and it is the TURBOQUANT FORK'S OWN contributor policy. Our AGENTS.md is our own governance file; carrying another project's contributor policy is a governance overwrite, not a capability. Zero engine content. THE 25 CAPABILITY ROWS lane-154 left 'NOT attempted' ARE NOW RULED, in place, in research/local-inference/2026-08-18-turboquant-disposition.md, each with its own verdict: 18 are DUPLICATE-AT-TIP (zero lines both missing here AND alive at turboquant/HEAD - lane-154's test under-reports for a fork that later replaced its own lines, and lane-154 took the moe-cache cluster at tip state), 1 TAKEN (f58ee0e97, a LIVE defect in our own tests/test-backend-ops.cpp init_tensor_uniform: a packed ggml_backend_tensor_set laid non-contiguous rows at i*row_size instead of i*nb[1]; commit c44d68931), 2 DEFERRED WITH NAMED BLOCKERS (e130aef60's 57 lines of server prompt-checkpoint sidecar are blocked on turboquant's TWO-BUFFER common_prompt_checkpoint data_tgt/data_dft vs our upstream single-buffer shape - a common/ struct port, not a delta; 5f5ef77ad's 8 copy_to_quant.comp bound-guard lines are blocked on a differential SET_ROWS case whose ne is not a multiple of gpr*ne21*ne22*ne23, which the suite does not contain), and 4 DECLINED with evidence (637300387/b43efe599/273bcc630 because OUR TREE IS AHEAD - we have the mul_mat_vec_id_tq{3,4}_1s pipelines their stopgap predates; f2d7f9303 because its whole live remainder is one CUDA mmvq line and one trivial test line). 9421bd097 IS DECLINED TWICE OVER: it is an abandoned pre-WHT WIP (489 lines of CENTROIDS_1BIT random-rotation design against the 1034-line WHT design at their tip and the 1040-line WHT design we already carry, all 53 of its missing lines DEAD at their own tip) AND it writes GGML_TYPE_TURBO3_0 = 43, which is OUR GGML_TYPE_Q2_0_G128. FLAG E RE-VERIFIED AT THIS TIP: ours are Q2_0_G128=43, TURBO2_0=200, TURBO3_0=201, TURBO4_0=202, COUNT=256; turboquant's own tip has drifted FURTHER into our space since lane-154 (TURBO2_0=43, TURBO3_0=44, TURBO4_0=47), which is precisely why the remap exists. PROOFS: research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-08-18-lane-156-currency2-proofs/",
       "pin_review": "lane-110C turbokv matrix (trial-evidence/110/turbokv-matrix.json) measured this tree end-to-end; WHT non-interchangeability proven against it (RESUME finding 4). That measurement was of c26cbdffc's LINEAGE - see the lane-143 key for why the sha moved and why the claim survives.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "THE OLD PIN WAS NOT MERELY BEHIND, IT WAS ON A LINEAGE THE FORK'S HEAD NEVER TOOK. c26cbdffc is 'Merge pull request #225 from TheTom/fix-ui-assets-partial-dist' (2026-07-18). `git branch -r --contains c26cbdffc` returns exactly two refs, turboquant/fix/vulkan-turbo3-flat-dequant-241 and turboquant/tom/merge-upstream-dsv4 - it is NOT contained by feature/turboquant-kv-cache, which is what origin/HEAD resolves to. merge-base(c26cbdffc, head) = 1fd6dfe9f, an UPSTREAM UI commit from 2026-06-14, and rev-list --left-right --count gives 338/841. So any 'c26cbdffc..head = 841 commits behind' figure is divergent-history arithmetic, not a delta. Re-pinned to f6124e914 (2026-08-17). The lane-110C claim above SURVIVES the move: the TurboQuant KV/WHT surface it measured is intact at the head, so this was a stale pin, not an evaporated finding. MEASURED DELTA from the merge-base: 816 non-merge, of which 151 are fork-authored (--not upstream/master) and 33 touch turbo/TQ quant or kernels; the other ~118 are upstream sync, DeepseekV4/DSpark, UI and CI. WHAT WE TAKE, ranked. (1) 7f8302613 'ggml-cpu : declare turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size extern, not a second definition' (2026-08-07) plus follow-up c7d6442dd (2026-08-12) - NO-OP FOR US, take only for tidiness. SELF-REFUTATION, recorded because this lane first wrote the opposite and the correction is the valuable part: I initially read recut's ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:26 `GGML_API int turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size;` as a SECOND DEFINITION in libggml-cpu against the real one in ggml-turbo-quant.c:31-32, and called it a live defect on our Windows DLL build on the strength of the fix's own commit message ('ELF interposition may merge them; two-level-namespace and DLL targets will not'). THAT WAS WRONG, and the error was not expanding the macro. In recut/2026-08-16:ggml/include/ggml.h, GGML_API expands to `... extern` in ALL FOUR branches (dllexport extern / dllimport extern / visibility-default extern / bare extern), so ops.cpp:26 is a DECLARATION on every platform and every build mode, and no second definition exists anywhere in our tree. Worse for the original framing: at turboquant's own pre-fix commit 7f8302613^ only the NON-Windows branch lacked `extern` (`__attribute__((visibility(\"default\")))` with no extern), so their bug lived on ELF/macOS and their commit message has the platform exactly BACKWARDS - the Windows branches already carried extern. Our tree is correct as it stands; these two commits change nothing for us. (2) cd4c3a1f6 'remove the per-call mallocs from the TurboQuant vec_dot kernels' (CPU, pure win). (3) e130aef60 'close complete-audit findings - 7 port regressions + TQ4_1S dp4a kernel' (an audit of exactly the port we did). (4) The Vulkan cluster of 2026-08-03/04, our backend: 844678bf2 SET_ROWS block decomposition for turbo weight types, 160649054 TQ MUL_MAT_ID size gate limited to the f16 dequant fallback, 5f5ef77ad TQ4_1S pipeline wiring, 4f2013d66 turbo3 KV pipeline, b43efe599 turbo3 wiring correction, 353ac109e + 637300387 mul_mat_vec_id add / MUL_MAT_ID reject, b514ae496 TQ3_1S weight type, b0c39adac TQ4_1S wiring restored - our merge 70a752991 post-dates these so several are probably already in, and EACH needs a content diff before cherry-picking (per-commit tree comparison across a rebase is a build lane's job, not a register lane's). (5) f050a2501 + a70a324fa fattn-vec turbo-K split for a VGPR spill, re-gated on the LUT rather than on D - authored for HIP/CUDA, but the gating correction is architecture-general. WHAT WE SKIP AND WHY: 3243b2875 (fused TQ3_1S mul_mat on HIP gfx1100 - our rig is a 780M gfx1103 on Vulkan, not HIP), 8365224ee (CUDA-only garbage-output fix), ffc210bfb (arm64 CI), 07e01ec54 + ce3dce77b + aab782c1b (DeepseekV4/DSpark model support - a different slot), and the ~118 upstream-sync commits which arrive with the next upstream move. CONTRACT CHECK: CLEAN. This head defines TQ3_1S=45 and TQ4_1S=46, exactly the ids